Currently `numpy.savetxt` uses old %-formatting to format strings. But old formatting doesn't support some new features. For example: a control of negative zeros ([PEP-682](https://peps.python.org/pep-0682/)), or a binary output (#20755). It would be great to support new formatting style via `str.format()`. Probably a good way to ask for a new formatting would be to use column `:` character instead of percent `%` as a first character of the formatting string.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/27994/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/27994/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},"comment":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/comments/2543363396","html_url":"https://github.com/numpy/numpy/issues/27994#issuecomment-2543363396","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/27994","id":2543363396,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAA3dP86XmKVE","user":{"login":"eendebakpt","id":883786,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4Mzc4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/883786?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt","html_url":"https://github.com/eendebakpt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/eendebakpt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-14T22:29:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-14T22:29:40Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"This seems like a reasonable request. We would have to preserve binary compatibility, but detecting whether the first character is a colon might be ok.  Another option would be to add a new keyword argument `fstring_fmt` (with default value `None`) that would override the old style formatting. It would have to support the same functionality has the current formatter (e.g. handle complex types)

@PavelStishenko Would you be interested in making a PR?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/numpy/numpy/issues/comments/2543363396/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}}

