This also fixes an edge case in numpy/ma/core.py::allequal where calling the function on the same input (i.e. `allequal(x, x)`) where the input is an unmasked array (i.e. `mask=np.ma.nomask`) would return `False`. The fix involves updating the `np.ma.mask_or` function to call `_shrink_mask` on the mask returned in this case. See issue #27201.
